- Created public GitHub repository `Data-Wise/savant-openai`.
- Added `origin` and pushed `feature/bootstrap-savant-openai` at `f5d3997`.
- Prepared `dev` as the integration branch from the current feature tip;
  publication remains a separate gate.
- Configured GitHub default branch to `dev`.
- Applied the documented protection baseline to `dev`: pull requests required,
  zero required approvals, admin enforcement, resolved conversations, and no
  force-pushes or branch deletion.
- Added the CI baseline plan and TODO.
- Added the read-only GitHub Actions CI workflow and repository-local skill
  validator.
- Completed CI dogfood on PR #4: the `test` job passed with 28 tests, 3 skill
  validations, and pull-request whitespace checks.
- Confirmed the stable observed job name is `test`.
- Required `test` with strict updates on protected `dev`.
- Merged PR #4 as `1508d4c` and verified the post-merge `dev` CI run passed.
- Completed runtime Codex evaluation on 2026-08-06: the `savant-research-verify`
  skill ran in actual `codex exec` sessions on the three fixture classes
  (positive, negative, unavailable-backend), baseline and lesson-assisted.
  All 6 runs produced the expected verdict, the approved lesson preserved every
  baseline verdict (no false `VERIFIED`), and the model correctly ignored the
  out-of-scope lesson. Recorded actual model token usage per run.
- Merged PR #6 as `cbdfb9f`: recorded the runtime Codex evaluation, applied the
  review amendments (evidence-path variance, transcript-archival limitation,
  cache-wording fix, pinned commit), and added the runtime evaluation
  follow-up plan. Merged with an admin bypass during the 2026-08-06 GitHub
  Actions outage; the post-merge `dev` CI run is pending GitHub recovery.
- Completed runtime evaluation follow-up Phases 1–2 (schema 1.2 evidence-path
  tracking and the committed deterministic CAS check). Runtime measurements
  now record a per-run `evidence_path` and flag any sub-CAS `VERIFIED`;
  `scripts/verify/symbolic-check.py` (SymPy 1.14.0) verifies proof fixtures
  deterministically in CI. Suite now passes 42 tests.
- Completed runtime evaluation follow-up Phase 3 (transcript archival policy):
  sanitized verdict excerpts from the 2026-08-06 evaluation are archived under
  `docs/measurements/logs/runtime-codex-2026-08-06/`; full raw dumps are
  explicitly non-archived per
  `docs/architecture/TRANSCRIPT-ARCHIVAL-POLICY.md`, enforced by
  `scripts/verify/sanitize-transcript.py` and gate tests. Suite now passes 47
  tests.
- Completed runtime evaluation follow-up Phase 4 (in-scope lesson fixtures):
  added `tests/fixtures/cancellation-without-assumption.json`, ran the
  baseline-versus-lesson matrix in `codex exec` (both `FAILED`), and recorded
  the lesson's in-scope effect (explicit rule application and missing-assumption
  naming) in `MEASUREMENT-in-scope-lesson-2026-08-06.md`.

